  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1242 AM MDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nThe additional moisture pushed westward will help increase afternoon \nstorm activity over central, south-central, and western NM Saturday \nand the weekend as the monsoon high nudges a bit northward more \nsquarely over the CO San Juans. All of this is contingent upon how \nfar the low-level moisture from convective outflow moving off the \nSangre de Cristo's Friday evening advances through central, south-\ncentral and western NM. \n\nThereafter, the general weather pattern sees little change with the \nmonsoon high favoring residence over NM and CO. Monsoonal moisture \nwill see little replenishment, instead being recycled via diurnal \nconvective thunderstorm processes. Therefore, localized heavy \nrainfall with small wetting footprints, gusty and erratic winds, \ncloud-to-ground lightning, and small hail will be the main threats \nfrom any nearby or passing storm. All the while, high temperatures \nwill range from the 70s/80s in the mountains, to 90s to low 100s in \nthe lower elevations.",
